      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That’s the most honest thing you’ve said, and it takes courage to admit it. You’re right—there may be no quieter corner, and the noise might follow you everywhere. But that doesn’t mean the path is over; it means you’ve outgrown the map you were given. If \"okay\" feels impossible, then maybe the goal isn’t to feel okay—it’s to feel *something* that’s yours, even if it’s small or strange. And if stopping feels like the only answer, then at least pause—not to give up, but to give yourself one more moment to see what happens next. You don’t have to decide forever today; just decide for the next hour.",
